{"id":"HKF-094","kind":"appraisal","key":"D07","status":"PARTIAL","finding":"PARTIAL: Uses hardware-profiled latency/accuracy (Tables II-IV) and probabilistic 3D LoS/NLoS path-loss with elevation angle and fast fading; however, omits Sim2Real factors (OS scheduling jitter), battery voltage sag, explicit UAV mobility trajectories, and dedicated fault-injection tests.","evidence":[{"page":10,"section":"VI.A. Experimental Setup","quote":"Other Sim2Real factors (e.g. OS scheduling jitter) are"},{"page":12,"section":"VI.B. Performance Analysis","quote":"under varied permissible delay thresholds do not serve"}],"note":""}
{"id":"HKF-094","kind":"appraisal","key":"D08","status":"PARTIAL","finding":"PARTIAL: Conclusions match profiled simulation/testbed comparisons and note missing battery voltage sag and fault-injection tests, but claim superior performance broadly without reporting numeric margins or separating testbed-only from simulation results.","evidence":[{"page":13,"section":"VII. CONCLUSIONS","quote":"demonstrated its superior performance compared to existing baseline"},{"page":13,"section":"VII. CONCLUSIONS","quote":"We will also design explicit fault-injection test settings to"}],"note":""}
{"id":"HKF-094","kind":"appraisal","key":"D09","status":"NOT_REPORTED","finding":"NOT_REPORTED: Checked Section VI.A, Section VII, Acknowledgments, and References; no author code repository, trained weights, or dataset release link is provided. Only third-party video [33] and Wikipedia workload [34] sources are cited.","evidence":[{"page":10,"section":"VI.A. Experimental Setup","quote":"For experimental video materials, we use urban traffic"},{"page":14,"section":"REFERENCES","quote":"[33] J. Utah, ”Traffic Camera Videos and Dash"}],"note":""}
{"id":"HKF-094","kind":"appraisal","key":"D10","status":"PARTIAL","finding":"PARTIAL: Explicitly discloses Sim2Real limitations (unmodeled OS scheduling jitter, battery voltage sag, lack of dedicated fault-injection tests) and lists NSFC/Shandong funding in Acknowledgments, but includes no conflict-of-interest or ethics declaration.","evidence":[{"page":10,"section":"VI.A. Experimental Setup","quote":"modeled in our current simulation, which constitutes a"},{"page":13,"section":"ACKNOWLEDGMENTS","quote":"This work is supported by the Shandong Provincial"}],"note":""}
{"id":"HKF-094","kind":"outcome","key":"Q01","status":"VERIFIED","finding":"Observed metric: original accuracy (unitless ratio) for fasterrcnn mobilenet 320 across resolutions: 0.4256 (1080P), 0.4098 (720P), 0.3911 (480P), 0.3845 (360P), 0.3508 (240P). Comparators: fasterrcnn mobilenet, retinanet resnet-50, maskrcnn resnet-50. Condition: urban traffic footage [33], hardware-profiled.","evidence":[{"page":10,"section":"VI.A, Table II","quote":"fasterrcnn mobilenet 320 0.4256 0.4098 0.3911 0.3845 0.3508"}],"note":""}
{"id":"HKF-094","kind":"outcome","key":"Q02","status":"VERIFIED","finding":"Observed metric: hardware-profiled computing time (seconds) at 1080P for fasterrcnn mobilenet 320: 0.451s on UAV (DJI Manifold, Table III) and 0.032s on EC (dual Xeon 4210R + RTX 4080, Table IV). Comparators: 3 other DNNs across 5 resolutions.","evidence":[{"page":10,"section":"VI.A, Table III","quote":"fasterrcnn mobilenet 320 0.451s 0.293s 0.186s 0.156s 0.131s"},{"page":10,"section":"VI.A, Table IV","quote":"fasterrcnn mobilenet 320 0.032s 0.019s 0.012s 0.011s 0.009s"}],"note":""}
{"id":"HKF-094","kind":"report_coverage","key":"coverage","status":"VERIFIED","finding":"VERIFIED_EXACT for Tables II-IV (p. 10, profiled original accuracy and UAV/EC computing times); PLOT_ONLY for main comparative and ablation outcomes in Figs. 3-6 (pp. 11-12, no printed numeric values for RUVA vs. baselines in prose or tables).","evidence":[{"page":10,"section":"VI.A. Experimental Setup","quote":"Quantitative evaluations of detection precision and computational latency"},{"page":11,"section":"VI.B. Performance Analysis","quote":"The performance comparison of our algorithm with other"}],"note":""}
{"id":"HKF-094","kind":"technical","key":"t2_decisions_objective_solver","status":"VERIFIED","finding":"Decisions: per-UAV binary offloading xn(t), resolution vn(t), DNN model mn(t). Objective: maximize long-term average inference accuracy IAn(t)=Rn(t)*1{Tn<=Tmax}*Am,v. Constraints: Tn<=Tmax, En<=Emax_n, xn in {0,1}. Solver: RUVA MARL (Dec-POMDP, QMIX-style factored critic, centralized policy gradients, Straight-Through Gumbel-Softmax). Missing: numeric Emax_n, Pu, Wn, pn.","evidence":[{"page":6,"section":"IV.A. Problem Formulation","quote":"where the goal is to maximize the long-term"},{"page":8,"section":"V.B. Centralized Policy Gradients","quote":"a deterministic policy-based centralized gradient estimator that performs"}],"note":""}
{"id":"HKF-094","kind":"technical","key":"t2_partition","status":"VERIFIED","finding":"Binary whole-task offloading (no DNN layer splitting): each UAV either executes the full selected DNN model locally (xn(t)=0) after on-UAV frame preprocessing or offloads the preprocessed frame to the single EC (xn(t)=1). Task assignment follows FIFO queues per node.","evidence":[{"page":4,"section":"III.A. Framework Description","quote":"perform the inference at the UAV or remotely"},{"page":6,"section":"III.D. Remote Computing","quote":"where xn(t) = 0 represents local computing and"}],"note":""}
{"id":"HKF-094","kind":"technical","key":"t2_topology","status":"VERIFIED","finding":"Two-tier star topology: N autonomous UAVs (3 DJI drones with Manifold onboard in testbed) wirelessly connected to one ground Edge Cloud server (EC); decentralized execution per UAV controller with offline centralized training (CTDE) on EC. No inter-UAV links or higher cloud tier.","evidence":[{"page":4,"section":"III.A. Framework Description","quote":"video frame processing and analysis comprising N UAVs"},{"page":10,"section":"VI.A. Experimental Setup","quote":"There were three Da-Jiang Innovations drones equipped with"}],"note":""}
{"id":"HKF-094","kind":"technical","key":"t2_workload","status":"VERIFIED","finding":"Workload: object detection on urban traffic footage [33] across 5 resolutions (1080P-240P) with request arrivals scaled from Wikipedia access logs [34]. Models: Faster R-CNN MobileNet (320 & standard), RetinaNet ResNet-50, Mask R-CNN ResNet-50. Baselines: MBF, SOA, CSL, CLH, ESL, ELH, NMN, IPG.","evidence":[{"page":10,"section":"VI.A. Experimental Setup","quote":"our video analytics experiment employs four"},{"page":11,"section":"VI.A. Experimental Setup","quote":"The static strategies (CSL, CLH, ESL, ELH) are"}],"note":""}
{"id":"HKF-094","kind":"technical","key":"t3_network_event_response","status":"PARTIAL","finding":"Models probabilistic 3D LoS/NLoS path loss with elevation angle and fast fading, plus Poisson computation/transmission soft-error failure rates (alpha in [0,0.1], beta in [0,0.03]); hardware failure sets high failure rate to mark UAV offline. Missing: mobility trajectories, handovers, fault-injection tests.","evidence":[{"page":5,"section":"III.B. Reliability Model","quote":"the system treats the UAV as offline and"},{"page":11,"section":"VI.A. Experimental Setup","quote":"tracks 3D distance and elevation angles to capture"}],"note":""}
{"id":"HKF-094","kind":"technical","key":"t3_platform_modality","status":"VERIFIED","finding":"Hybrid modality: physical hardware profiling (Tables II-IV) on 3 DJI Manifold UAVs and an EC (dual Xeon 4210R, RTX 4080, Ubuntu 20.04, PyTorch) parameterizes offline MARL simulation training (20,000 episodes); trained weights deployed to testbed, though Figs. 3-6 are simulation-driven.","evidence":[{"page":10,"section":"VI.A. Experimental Setup","quote":"noted that the training and physical deployment"},{"page":11,"section":"VI.A. Experimental Setup","quote":"measured from the physical hardware. Tables II-IV"}],"note":""}
{"id":"HKF-028","kind":"appraisal","key":"D01","status":"VERIFIED","finding":"YES: Clearly defines LLM-based UAV swarm path planning in Industry 5.0 rescue scenarios with N=M-1 UAVs running small quantized LLMs, one cloud large LLM, 2D fixed-altitude kinematics, uplink channel, LLM TTFT/TPOT/FLOPs cost model, and MSDTMD-SG + scene memory replay.","evidence":[{"page":6,"section":"3.1 System Overview","quote":"Each UAV acts as an edge server, providing"}],"note":""}
{"id":"HKF-028","kind":"appraisal","key":"D02","status":"VERIFIED","finding":"YES: States fixed altitude H=20m, negligible cloud-to-UAV return size, speed bounds Vmin<=Vk(t)<=Vmax, total bandwidth<=Bmax, total transmit power<=Pmax, solar harvesting model (Eq. 5, unused in P), and symbolic grid perception.","evidence":[{"page":6,"section":"3.2 UAV Control Model","quote":"We assume that all UAVs are at the"},{"page":9,"section":"3.5 Formulation of the Problem","quote":"total bandwidth allocated to all UAVs does not"}],"note":""}
{"id":"HKF-028","kind":"appraisal","key":"D03","status":"PARTIAL","finding":"PARTIAL: Specifies 20mx20m 1m grid, 10 UAVs, 8% obstacles, H=20m, Table 1 radio/speed params, RTX 4090/i7-14700K, Python 3.10/PyTorch 2.4.1/Unsloth 2025.2.15, LoRA r=128/alpha=16, temp=0.9, 20k train/5k eval samples; omits perceived diameters n_k, reward factors, prompt templates, and baseline hyperparameters.","evidence":[{"page":14,"section":"6.1 Experiment settings","quote":"We simplify the EC rescue scenario as a"},{"page":14,"section":"6.1 Experiment settings","quote":"During the LoRA [15] fine-tuning process with Unsloth,"}],"note":""}
{"id":"HKF-028","kind":"appraisal","key":"D04","status":"PARTIAL","finding":"PARTIAL: Compares 4 large LLMs, 3 4-bit small LLMs, 3 deployment schemes (large-only, hybrid, small-only), and DRL-USPP (DQN) plus ACO-USPP across 20 scenarios and 1,000 samples; however, ACO-USPP is capped at 100 iterations with local-only observation and baseline tuning details are omitted.","evidence":[{"page":15,"section":"6.1 Experiment settings","quote":"heuristic-based and DRL-based path planning algorithms, as detailed"},{"page":18,"section":"6.3 Performance Comparison of Different Methods","quote":"with only 100 iterations and limited local observations,"}],"note":""}
