{"id":"HKF-028","kind":"outcome","key":"Q02","status":"UNRESOLVED","finding":"UNRESOLVED: Fig. 4 (p. 15) prints 7 TPOT fractions (1/53, 1/103, 1/219, 1/181, 1/246, 1/272, 1/1170 s) across 7 LLMs, but PDFKit text loses bar-to-model mapping; TPOT for DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Llama-8B and LLaMA-3.2-3B cannot be reliably read from text alone.","evidence":[{"page":15,"section":"6.2, Fig. 4","quote":"Fig. 4. The TTFT and TPOP of different"},{"page":16,"section":"6.2 Performance Comparison of Different LLMs","quote":"Fig. 4 illustrates the TTFT and TPFT of"}],"note":"Bar labels in PDFKit text are vertically ordered and cannot be unambiguously assigned to individual models without visual PDF inspection."}
{"id":"HKF-028","kind":"report_coverage","key":"coverage","status":"VERIFIED","finding":"PLOT_ONLY (with PRINTED_UNRESOLVED bar labels in Fig. 4): All performance outcomes (Figs. 4-13, pp. 15-19) appear solely in figures with no numeric result tables or exact outcome values printed in prose (Table 1 lists only simulation parameters).","evidence":[{"page":16,"section":"6.2 Performance Comparison of Different LLMs","quote":"Fig. 5 and Fig. 6 show the path"},{"page":18,"section":"6.3 Performance Comparison of Different Methods","quote":"Fig. 11. The comparison of path planning performance"}],"note":""}
{"id":"HKF-028","kind":"technical","key":"t2_decisions_objective_solver","status":"VERIFIED","finding":"Decisions: next-step UAV waypoint P_k(t+1) and perception range/offload via link status zeta. Objective: minimize C_com+C_LLM (uplink delay/energy + LLM inference time/FLOPs). Constraints: speed [Vmin,Vmax], total bandwidth<=Bmax, total power<=Pmax. Solver: greedy search for MSDTMD-SG training samples + LoRA-SFT LLMs (Unsloth) + scene memory replay.","evidence":[{"page":8,"section":"3.5 Formulation of the Problem","quote":"formulated as an optimization problem P, which aims"},{"page":12,"section":"4.3 Multi-step Deep Thinking Learning for LLMs","quote":"use Unsloth AI’s open source fine-tuning framework Unsloth"}],"note":""}
{"id":"HKF-028","kind":"technical","key":"t2_partition","status":"VERIFIED","finding":"Binary model-level offloading (no DNN layer splitting) switched by cloud link status zeta: good link uploads max-range observation to cloud large LLM (DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Llama-8B); poor/no link shrinks perception range and runs onboard 4-bit small LLM (LLaMA-3.2-3B). Fine-tuning occurs in cloud; adapters distributed to UAVs.","evidence":[{"page":6,"section":"3.1 System Overview","quote":"upload the perceived information to the cloud, and"},{"page":14,"section":"5.2 Scene Memory and Replay Learning Mechanism","quote":"updated on the cloud and then the adapter"}],"note":""}
{"id":"HKF-028","kind":"technical","key":"t2_topology","status":"VERIFIED","finding":"Two-tier cloud-edge star topology: N=M-1 UAVs (10 UAVs in simulation) each acting as a mobile edge node with an onboard small LLM, communicating directly with 1 fixed-location cloud server hosting a large LLM. No inter-UAV links or multi-hop relay.","evidence":[{"page":6,"section":"3.1 System Overview","quote":"All LLMs are fine-tuned in the cloud using"},{"page":14,"section":"6.1 Experiment settings","quote":"The cloud server’s location is randomly assigned within"}],"note":""}
{"id":"HKF-028","kind":"technical","key":"t2_workload","status":"VERIFIED","finding":"Workload: multi-UAV grid path planning from local symbolic observation matrices; synthetic dataset via MSDTMD-SG (20,000 train, 5,000 eval samples; plus 20 scenarios and 1,000 local decision samples). Models: 4 large LLMs (selected DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Llama-8B), 3 4-bit small LLMs (selected LLaMA-3.2-3B). Baselines: DRL-USPP (DQN), ACO-USPP.","evidence":[{"page":15,"section":"6.1 Experiment settings","quote":"The fine-tuning dataset contains a total of 20,000"},{"page":16,"section":"6.2 Performance Comparison of Different LLMs","quote":"we select DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Llama-8B and LLaMA-3.2-3B"}],"note":""}
{"id":"HKF-028","kind":"technical","key":"t3_network_event_response","status":"PARTIAL","finding":"Wireless uplink uses 3GPP-style distance path loss and Shannon rate (B in [2,10] MHz, P in [100,200] mW, noise -110 dBm). Event response: poor cloud link triggers local small-LLM fallback with reduced perception; UAV damage logs scene memory for cloud replay fine-tuning. Missing: dynamic link transitions/handovers.","evidence":[{"page":6,"section":"3.1 System Overview","quote":"some UAVs may not be able to communicate"},{"page":13,"section":"5.2 Scene Memory and Replay Learning Mechanism","quote":"we store different memories for the cloud and"}],"note":""}
{"id":"HKF-028","kind":"technical","key":"t3_platform_modality","status":"VERIFIED","finding":"Pure software simulation on a lab server (Intel Core i7-14700K, 2x NVIDIA RTX 4090, Python 3.10, PyTorch 2.4.1, Transformers 4.49.0, Triton 3.0.0, Unsloth 2025.2.15) with 20mx20m grid; no physical UAV flight, HIL, or onboard edge hardware evaluation.","evidence":[{"page":14,"section":"6.1 Experiment settings","quote":"All experiments were conducted on our lab server"}],"note":""}
{"id":"HKF-029","kind":"appraisal","key":"D01","status":"VERIFIED","finding":"YES: Formulates outdoor multi-UAV collaborative task and path planning combining CTDE parameter-shared PPO (multi-objective reward: goal, avoidance, smoothness) with the UTTUT closed-loop control framework, P3 factor graph model, server-side Doubao-1.5-pro LLM, and onboard Grounding DINO RGB-D perception.","evidence":[{"page":3,"section":"3.1.2 Joint Policy Sharing and CTDE Mechanism","quote":"During training, a centralized Critic is used, which"},{"page":3,"section":"3.2 Multi-Agent Collaborative Task Planning","quote":"This section introduces the UTTUT framework and the"}],"note":""}
{"id":"HKF-029","kind":"appraisal","key":"D02","status":"PARTIAL","finding":"PARTIAL: Explicitly assumes known UAV localization/self-position, safety distance threshold d_safe for obstacle/inter-UAV avoidance, and factor-graph task synchronization constraints; however, omits UAV kinematics/dynamics bounds, battery/energy limits, and communication/latency constraints.","evidence":[{"page":3,"section":"3.1.1 Design of Multi-Objective Structured Reward Function","quote":"Negative rewards are given when the distance"},{"page":3,"section":"3.2 Multi-Agent Collaborative Task Planning","quote":"We assume that UAV localization is known and"}],"note":""}
{"id":"HKF-029","kind":"appraisal","key":"D03","status":"NO","finding":"NO: Reports host PC (i5-13600KF, 32 GB RAM, RTX 3090Ti), Python/PyTorch, AirSim, MATLAB, 3/6 UAVs, and 6/9 obstacles, but Section 5 explicitly admits omitting PPO architecture, training parameters, training procedures, reward weights, and scenario prompts.","evidence":[{"page":4,"section":"4 Experience","quote":"This platform has Intel Core i5-13600KF processor, 32"},{"page":5,"section":"5 Conclusion","quote":"detailed descriptions of the PPO model architecture, training"}],"note":""}
{"id":"HKF-029","kind":"appraisal","key":"D04","status":"PARTIAL","finding":"PARTIAL: Compares improved PPO against reimplemented PPO, DDPG, and SAC under unified state/action spaces in MATLAB (6/9 obstacles, 3/6 agents), and compares Centralization, Parallelism, Distribution, and Master LLM architectures in AirSim; however, baseline rewards follow original papers and architecture details are only schematic.","evidence":[{"page":5,"section":"4.1 Reinforcement Learning-Based Path Planning Experiments","quote":"All algorithms were trained and tested under the"},{"page":5,"section":"4.2 Multi-Agent Cooperative Task Planning Experiments","quote":"We compare centralization, parallelism, distribution, and master frameworks"}],"note":""}
{"id":"HKF-029","kind":"appraisal","key":"D05","status":"VERIFIED","finding":"YES: Path-planning metrics (average path length O., per-step inference time T., success rate S.) align with goal-reaching and avoidance rewards, and task-planning metrics (Success Rate, R-Time, C-Time) align with coordination speed and reliability; path smoothness is not directly quantified.","evidence":[{"page":5,"section":"4.1 Reinforcement Learning-Based Path Planning Experiments","quote":"Average path length (meters); T. Inference time per"},{"page":5,"section":"4.2 Multi-Agent Cooperative Task Planning Experiments","quote":"R-Time, response time for initial plan generation; C-Time,"}],"note":""}
